  "reason": "The study reports on the functional validation of a gene fusion in pediatric sarcomas using a cross-species comparative oncology approach. While it compares findings across zebrafish, mouse, and human samples, it does not report a quantitative measure of agreement between animal and human results (e.g., concordance rate, PPV, sensitivity/specificity). The focus is on delineating tumorigenic mechanisms and identifying therapeutic vulnerabilities, not on quantifying the translational accuracy of the animal models."
